ecially during high\u2011workload phases.\n- Whether A\u2019s leadership can mitigate his show\u2011off behavior and lack of demonstrated stress resilience.\n- The operational impact of B\u2019s weak numeric memory versus his stress handling.\n**What would change my vote**\n- Concrete evidence that C\u2019s communication or egocentric traits have caused crew conflicts or safety\u2011critical errors.\n- Strong evidence that A handles stress and remains calm under pressure while his show\u2011off attitude does not impair crew morale.\n- Evidence that B\u2019s numeric memory issue is effectively mitigated and his teamwork issues are minor.\nOverall, given the current balance of strengths and weaknesses, Candidate\u202fC best meets the reliability, technical competence, calmness, decision\u2011making, and teamwork criteria for long\u2011distance flights.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_3\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}"}
